Keys to the Cloud, Possibly in Stranger Hands
Access keys to cloud services may have fallen into the wrong hands. The cause is a compromise of a platform where developers trusted their secrets to rest. After spotting suspicious activity in its own infrastructure, the company warned all users to replace passwords, API keys, and other credentials at once. ezstandalone.cmd.push(function () { ezstandalone.showAds(153); });
What Railway Found
On October 21, Railway detected signs of unauthorized access to systems that store the environment variables of customer applications. Its review showed that outsiders could have obtained encrypted values. In some cases, they may also have seen decrypted content.
Environment variables often hold database passwords, API tokens, and access keys to private package registries. ezstandalone.cmd.push(function () { ezstandalone.showAds(161); });

