Service Status Update
By October 23, the service had restored builds and deployments for all plans, including Free and Trial. It kept a temporary ban on new sign-ups. Railway also began emailing customers with a high likelihood of compromise. ezstandalone.cmd.push(function () { ezstandalone.showAds(164); });
Several key facts remain undisclosed:

The exact number of affected accounts.
The method of initial entry.
The full scale of any leak.

The Scale of Potential Risk
The platform serves about 4.8 million users and more than 16 million services. Those figures do not mean every account was hit. Railway preliminarily estimates that only a limited share of customers is affected.
What Users Should Do Now
Even so, the company advises every customer to take three steps: ezstandalone.cmd.push(function () { ezstandalone.showAds(165); });

Replace stored secrets.
Revoke old keys.
Check service logs for suspicious activity.

